# Harness edit mode

Before changing harness structure, read `.cursor/shared/harness-principles.md`.

## Soft

- Clarify one module process; fix links/payloads; golden examples; INDEX sync.
- Add/edit **role-prefixed** conventions in the **owning** module (`eng-*`/`qa-*`/`sec-*`/`analyst-*`) + INDEX line; keep eng/sec/qa angles distinct.
- Tighten wording without meaning change.
- Add MCP server declaration without secrets + matching line in `shared/mcp-tools.md`.

## Hard (ask human)

- Add/remove/rename module; FSM/layers change; process outside `.cursor/`; fat root AGENTS.
- Peer-handoff; weaken evidence/self-close; alwaysApply loading all modules; duplicate canon into skills; second status SoR.
- Conventions in `shared/`/overlays/root; universal “for all roles”; unprefixed names that collide; leave old unprefixed beside new.
- Copy/fork across roles (`eng-test`↔`qa-test`, `eng-web`↔`sec-web`, …).
- Convention/constraints relay via OUTBOX; cross-read foreign conventions.
- Surfaces outside web/desktop/bots without human hard; empty convention stubs; alwaysApply on conventions.
- Secrets in `mcp.json`; unpinned `@latest` as default MCP package; always-on dangerous eval/XSS MCP; require MCP for bots/desktop without human; MCP policy/config inside `modules/*/conventions`.

## End checklist

- Principles read; placement ok; root thin; INDEX updated.
- Prefixed names; who reads/does not; process→conventions/INDEX; `surfaces[]` gate documented.
- eng≠qa≠sec angles; no stale unprefixed paths; size budget; changelog entry.
